/*
 * cpu/icache-place28 - icache-place27's slot load ahead of a cold target, by how the load's line was reached (jump / fall-through).
 *
 * WHY (2026-11-14; STATUS "pmsplit-sp's replay stamped at every visit"). pmsplit-sp's replay, stamped at every 386 instruction,
 * puts its gap in the segments that run many cold lines (~0.18 a line), where nearly every fill follows a taken branch or a jump,
 * often into a line's middle; every placement test before this one fell through from line to line. Each copy is two lines,
 * entered at word W of its first, with a branch (b = beq zero,zero / j / jr t0) at word B of its second and the delay slot
 * behind it, to word W of the next copy's first; 32 copies, the last to the return. Suffix: -ld a RAM lw in the delay slot,
 * -ldt a RAM lw at the target, -st a RAM sw in the delay slot. experiments/mk_place28.js writes this file (place27: -ld -93 over 32 copies with the load's line reached by falling through; icache-place10's one-line copies exact). Rows <K>L<LN>B<B>[-ld]: LN lines a copy.
 * READ IT LIKE THIS. Console - this core per row, cold and warm, over 32 copies.
 */
